  <hike>
    <date>2024-10-21</date>
    <place>Lac de Mauvoisin / Glacier d'Otemma / Lac de Crête Sèche, Switzerland</place>
    <pictures url="https://www.flickr.com/photos/bruchez/albums/72177720321753627"/>
    <image url="https://www.flickr.com/photos/bruchez/54121960494/in/album-72177720321753627/">2024-10-21 Lac de Mauvoisin - Glacier d'Otemma - Lac de Crête Sèche, Switzerland.jpg</image>
    <comments>A (very) long hike in the <i>Haut Val de Bagnes</i>. 10 hours. More than 36.5 km and 48,000 steps. I had never been to the vallon d'Otemma. It's a beautiful, desert-like area. During almost 3 hours, I was all alone in that large side valley (and without phone coverage). The Crête Sèche area is also quite nice. I just went to the lake. I'd like to go to the Col de Crête Sèche someday. That seems pretty doable (about 90 minutes from the lake).</comments>
  </hike>
